        <mxCell id="v57" value="&lt;b&gt;Notation (UML 2.5).&lt;/b&gt; Stick figure = actor outside the system; ellipse = use case; box = system boundary; plain line = association; hollow triangle = generalisation (Borrower and Lender are Booking parties, the primary actor of B12 and D1; every Booking party is a Member); dashed open arrow = &amp;#171;include&amp;#187; (always happens: B5 step 5, B12 step 4) or &amp;#171;extend&amp;#187; (conditional, from the extending use case to the base use case's extension point: B7 ext 3a, B8 ext 3a, D3/4/5 ext 4a).&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Not actors:&lt;/b&gt; the Trust Engine (Module 5) is part of the system. The Scheduler is the external timer that calls the job endpoint (UC-B13, ADR-0012); B13 carries out B6 *b (expiry), B7 *a (no-show) and B8 *a (overdue dispute) inside those use cases. D6 hands a case to I4 at D6 step 3 (no UML relationship). Colour = module: purple 1, blue 3, grey 4, green 5, yellow 7, orange 9." style="shape=note;size=12;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=10.5;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=4;fillColor=#F4F6F8;strokeColor=#8C99A6;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1350" width="1640" height="110" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
